## Core Categories of AI Skills

• Technical AI Skills: Building, testing, and managing AI models or infrastructure. This includes machine learning algorithms, data science, statistics, and programming languages like Python or Java.
• Non-Technical AI Literacy: Using AI tools effectively in everyday business tasks. This includes prompt engineering, critical thinking, responsible AI use, and cross-functional workflow automation.
• Modular AI Agent Skills: Reusable instruction files (like SKILL.md) that teach AI coding agents how to run tests, write code, triage issues, or interact with APIs.

